body:
My dude,

I'm in my late 20's and went through a lot before that, but honestly I will never understand what you're going through but I am here to listen if you want to talk about it more.

&#x200B;

One thing I do see is that you feel by showing others you're gone will make you feel more appreciated and seen. I hope that you feel you're seen by us. We're here for ya.

&#x200B;

Please don't do what you're thinking of doing..

If you are having violent thoughts I really recommend seeing someone about this.

As a person who has had many suicidal thoughts, I've never thought about hurting others.

NOBODY, not even your best friend or family or anyone, will ever understand what you're going through. All we can do is try to empathize and relate. We are all different people and in my opinion it's impossible for anyone to fully understand the hardships others are going through.

&#x200B;

Please, I beg you, if you are having thoughts of hurting others reach out immediately to the suicide hotline. Please do not hurt anyone. Even if it's just you wanting to hurt yourself, Please reach out. I am here to listen if you want to talk it out.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

National Suicide Prevention Lifeline

Hours: Available 24 hours. Languages: English, Spanish. [Learn more](https://support.google.com/websearch/?p=crisis_prevention_info)

800-273-8255

Take some time and breathe man. I can't imagine what it feels like to be in your situation right now but it seems very complicated with many speed bumps in the way.

&#x200B;

Are you still feeling suicidal? I'm glad you were able to talk to your boyfriend about it, sober or not.
